# Pin of the OpenVINO runtime that the llama.cpp OpenVINO pack builds against and ships.
# The llama.cpp source is not pinned here: the pack is one cell of the llama.cpp pack build and
# builds the same llama.cpp tag as the CPU, Vulkan, CUDA and ROCm cells. Both llama.cpp engine cache
# keys hash this file, so a runtime bump rebuilds every llama.cpp engine and renames its mirror asset.
#
# Upstream llama.cpp builds its OpenVINO release with OpenVINO 2026.4.1 (docs/backend/OPENVINO.md).
# This pin takes the RHEL 8 archive of that version: its libraries need glibc 2.27 and
# GLIBCXX_3.4.22, under the manylinux_2_34 floor of the pack. The Ubuntu 22 archive needs
# GLIBCXX_3.4.30, above that floor. The RHEL 8 archive holds the CPU, GPU and NPU plugins.
#
# The prebuilt runtime libraries are under the Intel OpenVINO Distribution License (the EULA in
# docs/licensing of the archive), not Apache-2.0, which covers only the headers, samples and Python
# API. The onetbb third-party notice names a GPL-3.0 code snippet with the GCC Runtime Library
# Exception. lilbee permits neither term, so the build script refuses to build until the owner
# accepts both (OPENVINO_LICENCE_RULING=accepted).
# OPENVINO_ARCHIVE_SHA256 is the digest that storage.openvinotoolkit.org publishes in the .sha256
# file next to the archive.
OPENVINO_VERSION=2026.4.1
OPENVINO_ARCHIVE_URL=https://storage.openvinotoolkit.org/repositories/openvino/packages/2026.4.1/linux/openvino_toolkit_rhel8_2026.4.1.22982.07f9c262b05_x86_64.tgz
OPENVINO_ARCHIVE_SHA256=db71613921217f52b2316acee6dc543d57ef54dd7c7c9241c575628b361c202e
# The release cell of the pack: the llama.cpp pack build runs this script for this cell.
OPENVINO_CELL=linux-x86_64-openvino
OPENVINO_BACKEND=openvino
OPENVINO_PLATFORM=manylinux_2_34_x86_64
OPENVINO_BUILD_SCRIPT=tools/wheel-build/llama_gpu_manylinux.sh
